    'body' => <<<'HTML'
<p>Houston is a city built for side income. It is enormous, it runs on cars, and it never really stops: refinery shifts, hospital shifts, port traffic, conventions, Rodeo season and a sports calendar that rarely goes quiet. Add no state income tax and housing costs well below most metros its size, and the best side hustles in Houston can pay off faster here than almost anywhere else in the country.</p>
<p>This guide covers 18 side gigs that work in Houston right now, what each one typically pays, what it costs to start, and the local details (neighborhoods, seasons, employers and events) that separate people who earn steady money from people who quit after a sweaty month.</p>

<div class="stat-row">
  <div class="stat"><b>0%</b><span>Texas state income tax</span></div>
  <div class="stat"><b>$15–$75</b><span>typical hourly range across these gigs</span></div>
